==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|revision|ism}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈvɪʒəˌnɪzəm/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|historiography}} The advocacy of a [[revision]] of some accepted [[theory]], [[doctrine]] or a [[view]] of [[historical]] [[event]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=January 22, 2020|author=Stuart Jeffries|title=Terry Jones obituary|journal=The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2020/jan/22/terry-jones-obituary|page=|text=As for Jones’s performance as Mandy Cohen, it united two leading facets of the funnyman’s repertoire: his fondness for female impersonation, and his passion for historical '''revisionism'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2018|author=Anne Perkins|title=A Dad’s Army-style Brexit looms. ‘Don’t panic!’|journal=Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2018/oct/08/brexit-dads-army-dont-panic
|passage=Tories spent last week boldly whistling their unique brand of the kind of historical '''revisionism''' that has played a major part in getting us here.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=Jan Grabowski|title=The New Wave of Holocaust Revisionism|work=The New York Times|date=2022-01-29|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/29/opinion/holocaust-poland-europe.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Meanwhile, Holocaust survivors are dying every day. There are few left to protest the new '''revisionism'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=w:Ezra Klein|title=It’s Time to Talk About ‘Pandemic Revisionism’|work=The New York Times|date=2023-08-29|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/29/opinion/ezra-klein-podcast-katelyn-jetelina.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Katelyn Jetelina is an epidemiologist and the author of the popular newsletter Your Local Epidemiologist. She argues that we’ve entered a new phase of the Covid-19 pandemic: “pandemic '''revisionism'''.”}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2025/03/enlightenment-trump-far-right-europe/682086/|title=A Battle for the Soul of the West|work=The Atlantic|date=2025-03-19|author=Arash Azizi|passage=For inspiration, they [Orbán’s fellow anti-liberal counterrevolutionaries] look to the Russia of Vladimir Putin, whose national chauvinism, banning of “gender ideology” and “gay propaganda,” and '''revisionism''' against the world order fit well with their agenda.}}
# {{lb|en|Marxism|derogatory}} An [[evolutionary]] form of [[Marxism]], abandoning some of its original principles.

